{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Pay student teachers at least the apprentice wage for compulsory placement hours",
        "additional_details": "Student teachers must complete compulsory school placements to qualify for QTS. These placements involve teaching, planning lessons, assessing pupils and other school responsibilities.\r\n\r\nUnlike salaried trainees, many university-based student teachers receive no wages for these hours. Placements can prevent them from working part-time while still having to cover travel and living costs.\r\n\r\nStudent maintenance loans are not wages for compulsory placement work. We therefore ask the Government to introduce a national scheme paying student teachers for placement hours at a rate equivalent to at least the applicable apprentice wage.\r\n\r\nPayment would recognise their time and contribution and make teacher training more accessible.",
        "background": "Require the Government to pay student teachers for compulsory school placements at a minimum rate equivalent to the apprentice wage. Payments should reflect hours completed, as placements are mandatory for qualifying as a teacher.",
